IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc26-interpretation`

-- ccc26-punishment.l4 -- sections 718.3 to 719 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: punishment generally, the minimum punishment,
-- and the commencement of a sentence and credit for time in custody (lines 15252-15308 of the text). Layer 1 of part ccc26.
-- The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation; it is not the official text and
-- nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Credit for time in custody is counted in days (a number the person states); a day count is right here because the text itself counts days.

§ `Section 718.3 -- Punishment generally`

-- (1) and (2): the court's discretion, within the enactment's limits. "Where" gate: the provision's own question, so a failed gate is JUST FALSE.
-- src:15252 | Punishment Generally
-- src:15253 | Degrees of punishment
-- src:15254 | 718.3 (1) Where an enactment prescribes different degrees or kinds of punishment in respect of an offence, the punishment to be imposed is, subject to the limitations prescribed in the enactment, in the discretion of the court that convicts a person who commits the offence.
@ref s 718.3(1) (src:15252-15254)
GIVEN `the enactment prescribes different degrees or kinds of punishment in respect of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the punishment is within the limitations prescribed in the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.3(1) the punishment is in the discretion of the court` MEANS   -- gate: where
    IF `the enactment prescribes different degrees or kinds of punishment in respect of the offence` AND `the punishment is within the limitations prescribed in the enactment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an enactment prescribes different degrees or kinds of punishment in respect of an offence, the punishment to be imposed is, subject to the limitations prescribed in the enactment, in the discretion of the court"

-- src:15255 | Discretion respecting punishment
-- src:15256 | (2) Where an enactment prescribes a punishment in respect of an offence, the punishment to be imposed is, subject to the limitations prescribed in the enactment, in the discretion of the court that convicts a person who commits the offence, but no punishment is a minimum punishment unless it is declared to be a minimum punishment.
@ref s 718.3(2) (src:15255-15256)
GIVEN `the enactment prescribes a punishment in respect of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the punishment is within the limitations prescribed in the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.3(2) the punishment is in the discretion of the court` MEANS   -- gate: where
    IF `the enactment prescribes a punishment in respect of the offence` AND `the punishment is within the limitations prescribed in the enactment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an enactment prescribes a punishment in respect of an offence, the punishment to be imposed is, subject to the limitations prescribed in the enactment, in the discretion of the court"

@ref s 718.3(2) (src:15256)
GIVEN `the enactment declares the punishment to be a minimum punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.3(2) the punishment is a minimum punishment` MEANS
    IF `the enactment declares the punishment to be a minimum punishment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no punishment is a minimum punishment unless it is declared to be a minimum punishment"

-- (3): imprisonment in default of payment of a fine where the enactment names no term: not more than the term prescribed for the offence.
-- The answer is the cap; NOTHING when the section sets none.
-- src:15257 | Imprisonment in default where term not specified
-- src:15258 | (3) Where an accused is convicted of an offence punishable with both fine and imprisonment and a term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine is not specified in the enactment that prescribes the punishment to be imposed, the imprisonment that may be imposed in default of payment shall not exceed the term of imprisonment that is prescribed in respect of the offence.
@ref s 718.3(3) (src:15257-15258)
GIVEN `the punishment the offence charged is liable to (from the offence section itself)` IS A Punishment
      `the offence is punishable with both fine and imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine is specified in the enactment that prescribes the punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
`s 718.3(3) the longest imprisonment in default of payment of the fine` MEANS
    IF `the offence is punishable with both fine and imprisonment` AND (NOT `a term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine is specified in the enactment that prescribes the punishment`)
    THEN JUST (`the punishment the offence charged is liable to (from the offence section itself)`'s `maximum imprisonment`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the offence is not punishable with both, or the enactment names a term, this section sets no cap and the enactment (or section 734) governs

-- (4): the court shall consider directing consecutive service. Two duties, and a list of cases it "includes".
-- src:15259 | Cumulative punishments
-- src:15260 | (4) The court that sentences an accused shall consider directing
-- src:15261 | (a) that the term of imprisonment that it imposes be served consecutively to a sentence of imprisonment to which the accused is subject at the time of sentencing; and
@ref s 718.3(4)(a) (src:15259-15261)
GIVEN `the accused is subject at the time of sentencing to a sentence of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court imposes a term of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.3(4)(a) the court must consider directing that the term be served consecutively to the sentence the accused is already subject to` MEANS
    IF `the accused is subject at the time of sentencing to a sentence of imprisonment` AND `the court imposes a term of imprisonment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that the term of imprisonment that it imposes be served consecutively to a sentence of imprisonment to which the accused is subject at the time of sentencing"

-- src:15262 | (b) that the terms of imprisonment that it imposes at the same time for more than one offence be served consecutively, including when
@ref s 718.3(4)(b) (src:15262)
GIVEN `terms of imprisonment are imposed at the same time for more than one offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.3(4)(b) the court must consider directing that the terms be served consecutively` MEANS
    IF `terms of imprisonment are imposed at the same time for more than one offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that the terms of imprisonment that it imposes at the same time for more than one offence be served consecutively"

-- The cases (b) "includes": a list that is not closed, so a case outside the four is NOTHING.
-- src:15263 | (i) the offences do not arise out of the same event or series of events,
-- src:15264 | (ii) one of the offences was committed while the accused was on judicial interim release, including pending the determination of an appeal,
-- src:15265 | (iii) one of the offences was committed while the accused was fleeing from a peace officer, or
-- src:15266 | (iv) one of the offences was committed with the use of violence, threats or attempts of violence against another person and the accused has been convicted, within the previous five years, of one or more such offences.
@ref s 718.3(4)(b)(i) (src:15263-15266)
GIVEN `the offences do not arise out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the offences was committed while the accused was on judicial interim release, including pending the determination of an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the offences was committed while the accused was fleeing from a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the offences was committed with the use of violence, threats or attempts of violence against another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been convicted of one or more such offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the accused's most recent conviction for such an offence` IS A DATE
      `the date the sentence is imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.3(4)(b) the case is one the paragraph names` MEANS
    IF    `the offences do not arise out of the same event or series of events`
       OR `one of the offences was committed while the accused was on judicial interim release, including pending the determination of an appeal`
       OR `one of the offences was committed while the accused was fleeing from a peace officer`
       OR (    `one of the offences was committed with the use of violence, threats or attempts of violence against another person`
           AND `the accused has been convicted of one or more such offences`
           AND `s 716 the earlier date falls within the five years up to and including the later date` `the date of the accused's most recent conviction for such an offence` `the date the sentence is imposed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including when"

-- (5), (6): what counts as a term or sentence of imprisonment for subsection (4); each "includes".
-- src:15267 | Cumulative punishments — fines
-- src:15268 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4), a term of imprisonment includes imprisonment that results from the operation of subsection 734(4).
@ref s 718.3(5) (src:15267-15268)
GIVEN `the imprisonment results from the operation of subsection 734(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.3(5) the imprisonment counts as a term of imprisonment for subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the imprisonment results from the operation of subsection 734(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a term of imprisonment includes imprisonment that results from the operation of subsection 734(4)"

-- src:15269 | Cumulative punishments — youth
-- src:15270 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (4), a sentence of imprisonment includes
-- src:15271 | (a) a disposition made under paragraph 20(1)(k) or (k.1) of the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985;
-- src:15272 | (b) a youth sentence imposed under paragraph 42(2)(n), (o), (q) or (r) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act; and
-- src:15273 | (c) a sentence that results from the operation of subsection 743.5(1) or (2).
@ref s 718.3(6) (src:15269-15273)
DECLARE `s 718.3(6) kind of sentence` IS ONE OF
    `s 718.3(6)(a) a disposition made under paragraph 20(1)(k) or (k.1) of the Young Offenders Act`
    `s 718.3(6)(b) a youth sentence imposed under paragraph 42(2)(n), (o), (q) or (r) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act`
    `s 718.3(6)(c) a sentence that results from the operation of subsection 743.5(1) or (2)`
    `s 718.3(6) a sentence of another kind`

@ref s 718.3(6) (src:15269-15273)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 718.3(6) kind of sentence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.3(6) the sentence counts as a sentence of imprisonment for subsection (4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 718.3(6)(a) a disposition made under paragraph 20(1)(k) or (k.1) of the Young Offenders Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.3(6)(b) a youth sentence imposed under paragraph 42(2)(n), (o), (q) or (r) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.3(6)(c) a sentence that results from the operation of subsection 743.5(1) or (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 718.3(6) a sentence of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a sentence of imprisonment includes"

-- (7): sexual offences against a child: the court shall direct consecutive service. "When" gate; JUST FALSE where it fails (the "(a)" and "(b)" limbs each).
-- src:15274 | Cumulative punishments — sexual offences against children
-- src:15275 | (7) When a court sentences an accused at the same time for more than one sexual offence committed against a child, the court shall direct
-- src:15276 | (a) that a sentence of imprisonment it imposes for an offence under section 163.1 be served consecutively to a sentence of imprisonment it imposes for a sexual offence under another section of this Act committed against a child; and
@ref s 718.3(7)(a) (src:15274-15276)
GIVEN `the court sentences the accused at the same time for more than one sexual offence committed against a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sentence of imprisonment is imposed for an offence under section 163.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sentence of imprisonment is imposed for a sexual offence under another section of this Act committed against a child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.3(7)(a) the court must direct that the section 163.1 sentence be served consecutively to the other sentence` MEANS
    IF     `the court sentences the accused at the same time for more than one sexual offence committed against a child`
       AND `a sentence of imprisonment is imposed for an offence under section 163.1`
       AND `a sentence of imprisonment is imposed for a sexual offence under another section of this Act committed against a child`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a court sentences an accused at the same time for more than one sexual offence committed against a child, the court shall direct"

-- src:15277 | (b) that a sentence of imprisonment it imposes for a sexual offence committed against a child, other than an offence under section 163.1, be served consecutively to a sentence of imprisonment it imposes for a sexual offence committed against another child other than an offence under section 163.1.
@ref s 718.3(7)(b) (src:15277)
GIVEN `the court sentences the accused at the same time for more than one sexual offence committed against a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sentence of imprisonment is imposed for a sexual offence committed against a child, other than an offence under section 163.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sentence of imprisonment is imposed for a sexual offence committed against another child, other than an offence under section 163.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.3(7)(b) the court must direct that the sentences for offences against different children be served consecutively` MEANS
    IF     `the court sentences the accused at the same time for more than one sexual offence committed against a child`
       AND `a sentence of imprisonment is imposed for a sexual offence committed against a child, other than an offence under section 163.1`
       AND `a sentence of imprisonment is imposed for a sexual offence committed against another child, other than an offence under section 163.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a court sentences an accused at the same time for more than one sexual offence committed against a child, the court shall direct"

-- (8) is shown repealed in this text.
-- src:15278 | (8) [Repealed, 2026, c. 12, s. 9]
@ref s 718.3(8) (src:15278)
`s 718.3(8), repealed` MEANS "[Repealed, 2026, c. 12, s. 9]"

§ `Section 718.4 -- Shorter term of imprisonment than minimum punishment`

-- (1) with (2): a minimum punishment of a specified term of imprisonment, which (2) says does not include life.
-- src:15279 | Shorter term of imprisonment than minimum punishment
-- src:15280 | 718.4 (1) When imposing a sentence for an offence that has a minimum punishment of a specified term of imprisonment, a court shall impose a shorter term of imprisonment than the specified term if, in the circumstances, the minimum punishment would amount to cruel and unusual punishment for that offender.
-- src:15281 | Exception — imprisonment for life
-- src:15282 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply with respect to an offence for which the minimum punishment is imprisonment for life.
@ref s 718.4(1) (src:15279-15282)
GIVEN `the minimum imprisonment the offence charged carries` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the minimum punishment would amount to cruel and unusual punishment for that offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.4(1) the court must impose a shorter term of imprisonment than the minimum` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the minimum imprisonment the offence charged carries`
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply with respect to an offence for which the minimum punishment is imprisonment for life"
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When imposing a sentence for an offence that has a minimum punishment of a specified term of imprisonment"
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN
        IF `the minimum punishment would amount to cruel and unusual punishment for that offender`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, in the circumstances, the minimum punishment would amount to cruel and unusual punishment for that offender"

-- src:15283 | For greater certainty
-- src:15284 | (3) For greater certainty, subsection (1) does not affect the operation of section 320.23.
@ref s 718.4(3) (src:15283-15284)
GIVEN `the provision in question` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.4(3) subsection (1) leaves the operation of the provision unaffected` MEANS
    IF `the provision in question`'s `section` EQUALS 320.23
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the clause says only that section 320.23 is unaffected

-- src:15285 | Reasons
-- src:15286 | (4) A court that imposes a shorter term of imprisonment under subsection (1) shall include in the record a statement of its reasons for doing so.
@ref s 718.4(4) (src:15285-15286)
GIVEN `the court imposes a shorter term of imprisonment under subsection 718.4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.4(4) the court must include in the record a statement of its reasons` MEANS
    IF `the court imposes a shorter term of imprisonment under subsection 718.4(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that imposes a shorter term of imprisonment under subsection (1) shall include in the record a statement of its reasons for doing so"

-- src:15287 | Minimum punishment
-- src:15288 | (5) For the purposes of this Part, the shorter term of imprisonment imposed under subsection (1) is a minimum term of imprisonment.
@ref s 718.4(5) (src:15287-15288)
GIVEN `the term was imposed under subsection 718.4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 718.4(5) the shorter term counts as a minimum term of imprisonment for this Part` MEANS
    IF `the term was imposed under subsection 718.4(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the shorter term of imprisonment imposed under subsection (1) is a minimum term of imprisonment"

§ `Section 719 -- Commencement of sentence; credit for time in custody`

-- src:15289 | Commencement of sentence
-- src:15290 | 719 (1) A sentence commences when it is imposed, except where a relevant enactment otherwise provides.
@ref s 719(1) (src:15289-15290)
GIVEN `a relevant enactment otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 719(1) the sentence commences when it is imposed` MEANS
    IF NOT `a relevant enactment otherwise provides`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where a relevant enactment otherwise provides"

@ref s 719(1) (src:15289-15290)
GIVEN `the day the sentence is imposed` IS A DATE
      `a relevant enactment otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 719(1) the day the sentence commences` MEANS
    IF NOT `a relevant enactment otherwise provides`
    THEN JUST `the day the sentence is imposed`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the day is the one the relevant enactment gives

-- src:15291 | Time at large excluded from term of imprisonment
-- src:15292 | (2) Any time during which a convicted person is unlawfully at large or is lawfully at large on interim release granted pursuant to any provision of this Act does not count as part of any term of imprisonment imposed on the person.
@ref s 719(2) (src:15291-15292)
GIVEN `the convicted person was unlawfully at large` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the convicted person was lawfully at large on interim release granted pursuant to a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 719(2) the time is excluded from the term of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the convicted person was unlawfully at large` OR `the convicted person was lawfully at large on interim release granted pursuant to a provision of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any time during which a convicted person is unlawfully at large or is lawfully at large on interim release granted pursuant to any provision of this Act does not count as part of any term of imprisonment"

-- (3): "a court may take into account any time spent in custody ... as a result of the offence": a grant whose object is limited by its own wording.
-- src:15293 | Determination of sentence
-- src:15294 | (3) In determining the sentence to be imposed on a person convicted of an offence, a court may take into account any time spent in custody by the person as a result of the offence but the court shall limit any credit for that time to a maximum of one day for each day spent in custody.
@ref s 719(3) (src:15293-15294)
GIVEN `the person spent the time in custody as a result of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 719(3) the court may take the time into account` MEANS   -- gate: none (the limit is on the time the grant reaches, not an "if")
    IF `the person spent the time in custody as a result of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any time spent in custody by the person as a result of the offence"

@ref s 719(3) (src:15293-15294)
GIVEN `the days spent in custody` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 719(3) the greatest credit, in days, for the time spent in custody` MEANS `the days spent in custody`

-- src:15295 | Exception
-- src:15296 | (3.1) Despite subsection (3), if the circumstances justify it, the maximum is one and one-half days for each day spent in custody.
@ref s 719(3.1) (src:15295-15296)
GIVEN `the days spent in custody` IS A NUMBER
      `the circumstances justify the exception` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 719(3.1) the greatest credit, in days, for the time spent in custody, when the circumstances justify it` MEANS
    IF `the circumstances justify the exception`
    THEN `the days spent in custody` TIMES 1.5
    ELSE `s 719(3) the greatest credit, in days, for the time spent in custody` `the days spent in custody`

-- src:15293 | Determination of sentence
-- src:15294 | (3) In determining the sentence to be imposed on a person convicted of an offence, a court may take into account any time spent in custody by the person as a result of the offence but the court shall limit any credit for that time to a maximum of one day for each day spent in custody.
-- src:15295 | Exception
-- src:15296 | (3.1) Despite subsection (3), if the circumstances justify it, the maximum is one and one-half days for each day spent in custody.
@ref s 719(3) and (3.1) (src:15293-15296)
GIVEN `the credit given, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the days spent in custody` IS A NUMBER
      `the circumstances justify the exception` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 719(3) the credit is barred as above the greatest the section allows` MEANS
    IF `the credit given, in days` GREATER THAN (`s 719(3.1) the greatest credit, in days, for the time spent in custody, when the circumstances justify it` `the days spent in custody` `the circumstances justify the exception`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court shall limit any credit for that time to a maximum of one day for each day spent in custody"

-- src:15297 | Reasons
-- src:15298 | (3.2) The court shall give reasons for any credit granted and shall cause those reasons to be stated in the record.
@ref s 719(3.2) (src:15297-15298)
GIVEN `credit was granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 719(3.2) the court must give reasons for the credit granted and have them stated in the record` MEANS
    IF `credit was granted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court shall give reasons for any credit granted"

-- src:15299 | Record of proceedings
-- src:15300 | (3.3) The court shall cause to be stated in the record and on the warrant of committal the offence, the amount of time spent in custody, the term of imprisonment that would have been imposed before any credit was granted, the amount of time credited, if any, and the sentence imposed.
@ref s 719(3.3) (src:15299-15300)
GIVEN `the record and the warrant of committal state the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record and the warrant of committal state the amount of time spent in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record and the warrant of committal state the term of imprisonment that would have been imposed before any credit was granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record and the warrant of committal state the amount of time credited, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record and the warrant of committal state the sentence imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 719(3.3) the record and the warrant of committal state what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `the record and the warrant of committal state the offence`
       AND `the record and the warrant of committal state the amount of time spent in custody`
       AND `the record and the warrant of committal state the term of imprisonment that would have been imposed before any credit was granted`
       AND `the record and the warrant of committal state the amount of time credited, if any`
       AND `the record and the warrant of committal state the sentence imposed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall cause to be stated in the record and on the warrant of committal the offence, the amount of time spent in custody, the term of imprisonment that would have been imposed before any credit was granted, the amount of time credited, if any, and the sentence imposed"

-- src:15301 | Validity not affected
-- src:15302 | (3.4) Failure to comply with subsection (3.2) or (3.3) does not affect the validity of the sentence imposed by the court.
@ref s 719(3.4) (src:15301-15302)
GIVEN `the court failed to comply with subsection 719(3.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court failed to comply with subsection 719(3.3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 719(3.4) the failure leaves the validity of the sentence unaffected` MEANS
    IF `the court failed to comply with subsection 719(3.2)` OR `the court failed to comply with subsection 719(3.3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Failure to comply with subsection (3.2) or (3.3) does not affect the validity of the sentence imposed by the court"

-- src:15303 | When time begins to run
-- src:15304 | (4) Notwithstanding subsection (1), a term of imprisonment, whether imposed by a trial court or the court appealed to, commences or shall be deemed to be resumed, as the case may be, on the day on which the convicted person is arrested and taken into custody under the sentence.
@ref s 719(4) (src:15303-15304)
GIVEN `a term of imprisonment is imposed by the trial court or the court appealed to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the convicted person is arrested and taken into custody under the sentence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 719(4) the day the term of imprisonment commences or is resumed` MEANS
    IF `a term of imprisonment is imposed by the trial court or the court appealed to`
    THEN JUST `the day the convicted person is arrested and taken into custody under the sentence`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a term of imprisonment, whether imposed by a trial court or the court appealed to"

-- src:15305 | When fine imposed
-- src:15306 | (5) Notwithstanding subsection (1), where the sentence that is imposed is a fine with a term of imprisonment in default of payment, no time prior to the day of execution of the warrant of committal counts as part of the term of imprisonment.
@ref s 719(5) (src:15305-15306)
GIVEN `the sentence is a fine with a term of imprisonment in default of payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time falls before the day of execution of the warrant of committal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 719(5) the time is excluded from the term of imprisonment in default of payment` MEANS
    IF `the sentence is a fine with a term of imprisonment in default of payment` AND `the time falls before the day of execution of the warrant of committal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the sentence that is imposed is a fine with a term of imprisonment in default of payment, no time prior to the day of execution of the warrant of committal counts"

-- src:15307 | Application for leave to appeal
-- src:15308 | (6) An application for leave to appeal is an appeal for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 719(6) (src:15307-15308)
GIVEN `it is an application for leave to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 719(6) the application counts as an appeal for section 719` MEANS
    IF `it is an application for leave to appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only what an application for leave to appeal is
